measures and give a Monte Carlo SE for each. The SE of the relative error
is a delta-method approximation. It assumes that the estimate is normal,
and that \code{se} is independent of the estimate. The SE of the coverage uses
\code{level}, not the observed share. Under a correct analysis the true share
is \code{level}, and the observed share is 1 in many small studies, which gives
an SE of 0.

